# Each phrase inflates a count without giving it, so the fix writes
# `many` or names the items (`a wide range of styles` becomes `the
# serif, sans, and mono styles`). The fix does not give the count,
# because a count of a set that can grow goes stale.
#
# `a host of` skips a following determiner (a word that introduces a
# noun, such as `the`, `a`, or `this`), where `host` names a machine (`a
# host of the cluster`). `various` skips `different`, because the
# redundant-pair rule reports `various different`, and the filter
# narrows the finding back to `various`.
expr main [(rich set), (wide range), (wide variety), (plethora of), (myriad of), (a myriad), (wide array), (vast array), (broad range), (diverse range), (a host of ![the, this, that, a, an, each, every, its, their]), (a whole host), (a slew of), countless, numerous, <(various !different), various>, (a variety of)]
let message "Vague quantity. Write many, or name the items."
let description "Flags phrases such as wide range and plethora of that inflate a count without giving it."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The catalog holds forty styles."
allows "The range covers ports 1 through 1024."
allows "Drain a host of the cluster before the upgrade."
